            "review_title": "Review at Vietnam Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Liz_D27\nBrisbane, Australia359 contributions\n0\nDelicious food at reasonable prices\nDec 2016\nWe had lunch here as the place we had intended to go was closed!\nWe decided on this place as there were lots of locals eating here even though it was after 13:30. The staff were friendly even though their English was minimal, it was still much better than my non-existent Vietnamese! There is an English menu which we quite happily ordered off. The food came out pretty quickly & was reasonably priced. We shared what we ordered as we wanted to sample a few different things.\nWe ordered stir fried vegetables, spring rolls (the serve was $6AUD which I thought was a bit steep until they bought the plate of spring rolls out - 10 rolls!!) & pork chop. The pork was more like ribs with bones but we weren't bothered as the pork was the highlight! It was smokey & the sauce was rich & delicious but not over powering. If my chopstick skills were superior I wouldn't have needed to use my fingers much at all! \n\nLunch was about $15AUD for the three plates & two soft drinks. I am sure we paid 'tourist prices' but we felt it was worth it.\nNot to mention it was a great place to stop & eat out of the pouring rain.\nRead more\nWritten December 19, 2016",
